      "key": {
        "uuid": "204a4409_9f157c64",
        "filename": "src/dawn/common/Algebra.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 214,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-05T16:52:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m pretty sure this is right with the tests and the usage in WIP CLs. We may have learned this stuff with different conventions, but what this does is doing a weighed sum of the column vector (aka the images of the basis vectors by A) by the coordinates of V. By linearity of matrix - vector multiplication, this should be the result of the multiplication. If basis vectors are `v0..vn` and `V \u003d a0 * v0 + ... + an * vn`, then\n\n```\n  A * V\n\u003d A * (a0 * v0 + ... + an * vn)\n\u003d a0 * A * v0 + ... + an * A * vn\n```\n\nthe latter is what we are computing in the function.",
      "parentUuid": "d4cc69c9_c3ab3b4c",
      "revId": "89cf7b0d46eee889018d7bb6804bc3d64d7a281f",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
